# CoachBuilder — agent workflow

## Default: always ship to Vercel (via Git)

- **User expectation:** From here on, **the agent** (not the user) does **commit + push** after meaningful edits, except when the user explicitly opts out (“não faças push”, “só local”, “não commits yet”). Do not assume the user will use Source Control or Terminal to push.
- **Unless the user explicitly says not to push** (e.g. “local only”, “don’t commit yet”), finish every substantive coding task by **committing and pushing** to `origin` on the branch Vercel watches. That push is what triggers **automatic Vercel deployment** — no separate “deploy to Vercel” button is required when Git integration is connected.
- Work in the **git root** for this app: the workspace folder **`CoachBrain`** is the same repo as [github.com/PedroSousa008/coachbuilder](https://github.com/PedroSousa008/coachbuilder) — Next.js lives at the **repo root** (`package.json`, `src/`), not in a nested `coachbuilder/` subfolder.

## Terminal and tooling

- **Do not** ask the user to run commands in their terminal. **You** run shell commands (`npm`, `git`, etc.) in the environment.
- Prefer **absolute paths** under the project when running commands, e.g. `/Users/pedrocastrosousa/Desktop/Sousa/CoachBrain`.

## Git and delivery

- After **meaningful code or config changes** (anything that should ship), run:
  1. `git status` / `git diff` as needed
  2. `git add -A`
  3. `git commit -m "<clear, conventional message>"`
  4. `git push origin main` (or the current default branch)
- If there is **nothing to commit**, do not create empty commits; still **push** if local commits exist that are not on `origin`.
- Resolve merge conflicts in the workspace if they appear; do not leave the branch broken.

## Vercel deployment

- This project is intended to deploy **automatically** when code reaches GitHub: [Vercel Git integration](https://vercel.com/docs/deployments/git) builds on every push to the connected branch (usually `main`).
- **Pushing to `origin/main` is the deploy trigger** — there is no separate “push to Vercel” step when the Vercel project is imported from [github.com/PedroSousa008/coachbuilder](https://github.com/PedroSousa008/coachbuilder).
- Only if Git integration is **not** used: deploy with Vercel CLI using a token already present in the environment (e.g. `VERCEL_TOKEN`), non-interactively. **Never** commit tokens or put them in the repo.

## If Vercel shows no new deployment after a push

Git pushes go to **GitHub** first. Vercel deploys only if the **Vercel project’s Git settings** match this repo and branch.

1. **Confirm GitHub has the commit**: open [github.com/PedroSousa008/coachbuilder/commits/main](https://github.com/PedroSousa008/coachbuilder/commits/main) — the latest commit should match what was just pushed.
2. In **Vercel → your project → Settings → Git**: **Connected Git Repository** must be `PedroSousa008/coachbuilder` (not another repo or fork). **Production Branch** must be `main` (or whatever you push to).
3. **Root Directory** must be empty or `.` — this app lives at the repo root, not inside a parent folder.
4. Open **Deployments**: if a deployment exists but is **Error**, open the build log (TypeScript/build failure). Fix the error, commit, push again.
5. If the repo was renamed or Git was disconnected: **Reconnect** the GitHub integration or **Import** the project again from the correct repo.
6. To force a new build: an empty commit + push can re-trigger the webhook: `git commit --allow-empty -m "chore: trigger Vercel"` && `git push origin main`.

## When the user asks for “deploy” or “ship it”

1. Ensure the app builds if possible (`npm run build`) when dependencies are available.
2. Commit and **push** to GitHub.
3. Confirm that Vercel will pick up the deployment from the push (no extra user terminal steps).
